SeaBIOS fixes for tiny386 on the ESP32-S31-Korvo-1
===================================================
Against SeaBIOS 81ec9ec0 (rel-1.17.0-20) with tiny386's own patch
(patches/seabios-tiny386.patch, tiny386 9ed786b) applied first:
tools/build-bios.sh applies the two in that order.  Found by
tests/bios-tests.sh; BIOS-COVERAGE.txt has the details.  What IBM's VGA and
its BIOS do is what is wanted.  Offered under the GNU LGPL version 3, as
SeaBIOS is.

vgasrc/stdvgaio.c, stdvga.h
  The attribute controller's flip-flop is reset by reading input status 1
  at 3BAh while the misc output selects monochrome addressing, and at 3DAh
  otherwise.  It was always 3DAh, which a VGA does not answer in mode 07h:
  the next mode set after 07h filled the palette registers askew, and every
  palette call in 07h went astray.

vgasrc/stdvgamodes.c
  * The mode set writes the misc output before the CRT controller, not
    after.  In mode 07h all 25 CRT controller registers went to 3B4h while
    the misc output still selected 3D4h, a VGA ignored them, and the screen
    was black.
  * 12h BL=30h AL=01h (350 scan lines) now does something: modes 00h to
    03h are then 8x14 characters in 350 lines, 8 dots wide (80 columns are
    640x350), and 07h 9x14 (720x350), as on IBM's VGA; the 8x14 font is
    loaded for them.  The vertical registers are those of modes 0Fh and
    10h, the horizontal those of the 400-line text modes.  8x8 (11h AL=12h)
    then gives 43 rows.  The video parameter table keeps the 400-line modes.

vgasrc/stdvga.c, stdvga.h
  stdvga_enable_video_refresh(): the sequencer's screen-off bit (SR01h bit 5).

vgasrc/vgabios.c, vgabios.h
  * Cursor emulation (01h) scales a CGA shape the way IBM's VGA BIOS does:
    0607h gives lines 13 and 14 of 16, which is what the mode set leaves;
    it gave 14 and 15.  Shapes that end below line 7, or are switched off,
    are left as they were.
  * 12h BL=31h (default palette loading) sets bit 3 of 0040:0089h, which
    the mode set reads; it set bit 3 of 0040:0087h.
  * 12h BL=36h (video refresh) sets and clears SR01h bit 5; it did nothing.
  * 10h AL=10h and AL=12h store greys while summing (12h BL=33h) is on.
  * 1Bh gives the rows (not the rows less one) and the colours, pages and
    scan lines of the mode in use; it gave 16, 8 and 400 for every mode.
  * 0Ch and 0Dh use the page in BH in the planar modes that have room for
    more than one (0Dh, 0Eh, 0Fh, 10h); they always used page 0.
  * A mode set after 200 scan lines were selected (12h BL=30h AL=00h, which
    SeaVGABIOS does not do: it sets 400) leaves 0040:0089h saying 400, so
    that the next one is not taken for 350.

vgasrc/vgafb.c, vgafb.h
  The pixel functions take the page; struct gfx_op has where it starts.

src/disk.c, src/hw/floppy.c, src/util.h
  13h AH=18h (set the media type for a format) on a floppy drive: accepted
  for a media that the drive takes, with ES:DI pointing at the diskette
  parameter table and the media noted in the BIOS data area as media
  sensing notes it; 0Ch for any other.  It was refused with 01h.

